window.docContents[44].resolve({"/Kernel-reassociation/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Kernel-reassociation--Example":{"contents":"The @[kernel_reassoc] attribute works the exact same way as @[reassoc], but for equalities of s-finite kernels:\n\n\n\n\n\nvariable {W : Type*} [MeasurableSpace W] (ξ : Kernel (Z × Z) W) [IsSFiniteKernel ξ]\n#check parallelComp_self_comp_copy'_assoc κ ξ\n\n\nparallelComp_self_comp_copy'_assoc κ ξ : ξ ∘ₖ (κ ∥ₖ κ) ∘ₖ copy (X × Y) = ξ ∘ₖ copy Z ∘ₖ κ\n\n\n","context":"Kernel-Hom: Tactics for Kernel Categorical Reasoning\u0009Kernel reassociation","header":"6.1. Example","id":"/Kernel-reassociation/#Kernel-Hom___-Tactics-for-Kernel-Categorical-Reasoning--Kernel-reassociation--Example"}});